{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 2706,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How much LSD should\nyou give an elephant?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2706,
    "dDurationMs": 1614,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\nWell, to a reasonable person,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4320,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the correct answer is probably none."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6720,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what if you needed to do\nit for a scientific experiment?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10400,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 1960s, the CIA was working on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12640,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a top secret project known as MKUltra,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15120,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and one of their main\ngoals was to find out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how drugs like LSD could be\nused to change human behavior."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21280,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is where elephants come in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23200,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because elephants are\nnormally quite docile,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25600,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but sometimes they just snap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27920,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the hypothesis was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29280,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that this change in\nbehavior might be triggered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31520,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the release of an LSD-like substance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33840,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that naturally occurs in their brains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if that's true, then administering LSD"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39120,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a docile elephant might\nreproduce that behavior."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42960,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the real question was\nhow much LSD should you give"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45440,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an elephant so that the\ndose is large enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47280,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to cause a psychological reaction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49200,
    "dDurationMs": 3666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but not so large that it causes harm?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52866,
    "dDurationMs": 14,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52880,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the researchers didn't\nknow, LSD had never been given"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56080,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to an animal that big,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57920,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they did know that\nthe safe dose in cats"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60400,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was around 0.3 milligrams."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, since an elephant has around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64720,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a thousand times the mass of a cat,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66400,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they figured we'll give it\na thousand times the dose."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They received approval to\nperform the experiment on Tusko,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an Indian elephant at the\nLincoln Park Zoo in Oklahoma."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76000,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there they injected him"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with nearly 300 milligrams of LSD."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80960,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But within five minutes,\nTusko trumpeted, collapsed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84480,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fell heavily onto his\nright side, defecated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87440,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and went into status epilepticus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90240,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They administered a few other drugs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92080,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in an attempt to revive him,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93680,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but Tusko died shortly thereafter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96800,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The mistake they made was to assume"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that safe drug dosage\nscales linearly with mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102560,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It does not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103760,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it turns out there are\na lot of things like this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106240,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that don't scale in the way you'd expect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108800,
    "dDurationMs": 400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109200,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, take the\nsmallest mammal by mass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112080,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Etruscan shrew,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113600,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the largest land mammal,\nthe African bush elephant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117120,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which do you think has more heartbeats"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119200,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the course of its entire life?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121760,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, an African elephant has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123360,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around a billion\nheartbeats in its lifetime,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and an Etruscan shrew also has a billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129760,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heartbeats in its lifetime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131600,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What about a wallaby?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133200,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also a billion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134240,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A two-toed sloth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135520,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A billion again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136800,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just about every mammal, no matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138880,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what environment they live\nin, how large they are,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or even whether they live\nfor one year or 100 years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they all get around a billion heartbeats"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between the day they're\nborn and the day they die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149280,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Why a billion?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150480,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why not a million?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151360,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why not a thousand?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152240,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not these other numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153800,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That is every mammal except one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157280,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video is in large\npart based on the book"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159520,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scale by Geoffrey West."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161120,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to learn more,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162160,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'll put a link to it\ndown in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164720,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's even more curious is that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166400,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just by knowing a mammal's mass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168240,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can predict a staggering number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170000,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of biological traits from its pulse rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172640,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and reproductive output\nto its total lifespan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176000,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same pattern holds for cities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178160,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you know the population and location,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that allows you to forecast\neverything from average wages"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182960,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and patent filings to crime\nrates, disease prevalence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186240,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even the literal speed\nat which pedestrians walk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190240,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how is that possible?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192240,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, for that, we have\nto go back to the case"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193680,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Tusko the Elephant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195440,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Researchers assumed that safe drug dosage"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197760,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is proportional to mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199040,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Double the mass, double the dose."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200880,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it turns out that the\nspeed at which an animal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203120,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can process chemical compounds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't depend directly on its mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207280,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It depends more on its metabolic rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209920,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the number of calories it uses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212240,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a given amount of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213560,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There's a lot going on in your body."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215840,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your heart is pumping, that takes energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218240,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You're moving food around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220400,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Digestion takes energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222240,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Keeping your brain going\ntakes energy, breathing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224800,
    "dDurationMs": 3017,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything that you do requires energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227817,
    "dDurationMs": 1863,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\n- [Host] For a cat, for a single day,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229680,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they require roughly 250\nkilocalories of energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233600,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "used by all of their trillions of cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236320,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is nothing\nspecial about a cat's cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239200,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you take a cat's cells\nand an elephant's cells"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241280,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and put them under a microscope,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242720,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll find they're a\nsimilar size, similar makeup,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245520,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they perform the\nsame sorts of functions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247840,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same is true for other animals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250000,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, the building blocks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251680,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of animals are always roughly the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254160,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So an elephant that has\na thousand times the mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256640,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has about a thousand times as many cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258960,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you'd expect it would need a thousand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261120,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times as much energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262400,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So 250,000 kilocalories per day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266080,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that is where you run into problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268280,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So what's the issue here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270160,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If I'm an organism"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271200,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I'm burning up energy all day long,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273680,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that energy is radiated out\nin the form of body heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277840,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we're constantly losing\nheat through our surface,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280800,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through our skin, to the environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283080,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- To see why this matters,\nlet's simplify the problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286000,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and do the standard physicist thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287920,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's assume our animals\nare perfect spheres."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291200,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To be clear, this isn't necessary\nfor the argument to work,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293760,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it does make everything\na lot easier to follow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296400,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since the volume of an animal\nis proportional to its mass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299440,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our 3000 kilogram elephant\nhas a volume a thousand times"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302480,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "greater than our three kilogram cat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304560,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So its radius must be 10 times larger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306880,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because volume is\nproportional to radius cubed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310000,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But surface area only\ngrows as radius squared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313040,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the elephant's surface area"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314560,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only increases by a factor of 100."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317040,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Generating a thousand times as much heat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while only having a hundred\ntimes the surface area"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to radiate it away would end very"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323280,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "poorly for the elephant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324640,
    "dDurationMs": 3906,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If this were the case,\nit would boil alive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328546,
    "dDurationMs": 1454,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\nSo in 1838,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330000,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "French scientists proposed\na different scaling law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332960,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since metabolism generates heat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334560,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that heat is radiated\nthrough the surface,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336640,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "metabolic rate or B,\nshould scale in proportion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339600,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the surface area, A, instead."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342160,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This became known as the surface law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344720,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, we can rewrite this to see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346240,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how metabolic rate scales\nas a function of mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348960,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Surface area is proportional\nto radius squared,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351520,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we can swap that in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352960,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if mass is proportional\nto radius cubed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355200,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then radius must be proportional\nto mass to the one-third."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358160,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plugging that in for R,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359280,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we find that metabolic rate should scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360880,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with mass to the two-thirds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362520,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Really familiar example would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364800,
    "dDurationMs": 2866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "come from thinking about cooking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367666,
    "dDurationMs": 14,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367680,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe you want to make a\nbig turkey for Thanksgiving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "People commonly phrase it as\nhow long do I need per pound?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373680,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that you realize is linear thinking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375520,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The important thing is really\nthe thickness of the bird"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the roast, because\nthe heat is coming in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381040,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by conduction from the oven"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384080,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's got to do thermal\ndiffusion into the meat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388240,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The time for the diffusion will scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390720,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the characteristic length,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392560,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which in this case would be\nthe thickness of the meat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394640,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It'll go like the dimension squared,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397040,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whereas volume of the meat is\ngoing to be like length cubed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401440,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's proportional to the weight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403280,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the bird or the roast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404640,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when you put those things together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406080,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll get that the characteristic\namount of time needed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408880,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to cook the roast will go like its mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411280,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the two-thirds power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412680,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So if I'm thinking about cooking a roast"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415440,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that weighs twice as much as\nanother roast, how much longer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418720,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is that two to the two-thirds the time?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421320,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, if you wanted\nto double the weight,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423760,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you only have to\ncook it about 60% longer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426960,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not 100% longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Host] Similarly,\naccording to this scaling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431280,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an elephant that's a thousand\ntimes as heavy as a cat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433760,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should only burn a hundred\ntimes as many calories."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So 25,000 instead of 250,000."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439840,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the appropriate dose of LSD for Tusko"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442480,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would've been just 30 milligrams."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445200,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These two wildly different\npredictions come from different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447920,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assumptions about how metabolic rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449600,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scales as a function of mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451520,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But notice in both cases,\nit's just proportional"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454160,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to mass raised to some power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456160,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These kinds of relationships\nare called power laws"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458640,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and all power laws have\na special property."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461200,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you take the logarithm\nof the X and Y values,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464320,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465920,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the slope of the line is equal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467440,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the exponent of the power law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469600,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This makes it easy to identify"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471280,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "different types of power laws."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the slope is one, that's\njust everyday linear scaling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If it's less than one,\nlike the surface law,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478320,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is called sublinear scaling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480320,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if it's larger than one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481920,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is known as superlinear scaling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484880,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For nearly a hundred years,\nbiologists generally agreed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487840,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the two-thirds exponent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489120,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the surface law was the\ncorrect one for metabolic rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492640,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then in 1932, Swiss\nbiologist, Max Kleiber,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496160,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decided to put it to the test."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497920,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He took the metabolic rates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499360,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of different animals from\na small dove at 150 grams"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502640,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a large steer at 680,000 grams,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then he plotted\nthem against their mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508000,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a log log plot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509520,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as expected, all the data\ndid fall on a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512960,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the slope wasn't two-thirds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515200,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, it was about three quarters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517920,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This became known as Kleiber's Law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520640,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It implies that if you\ndouble an animal's mass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522880,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "metabolic rate goes up by about 1.68,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525680,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an increase of 68% instead of the 59%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529040,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which would be predicted by\nthe two-thirds scaling law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531920,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So according to Kleiber's Law,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533360,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an elephant burns roughly 178 times"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as many calories as a cat,\nor about 45,000 kilocalories."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540000,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the actual LSD dose\nTusko should have received"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543040,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was 53 milligrams, which is\naround a sixth of the dose"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546800,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the researchers gave him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548400,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that explains the dosing catastrophe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550960,
    "dDurationMs": 2306,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with Tusko The Elephant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553266,
    "dDurationMs": 14,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553280,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kleiber's original work was\nbased on a small data set,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556160,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "primarily made up of mammals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558160,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you plot the data for\na larger range of mammals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561120,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well as for other animals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562480,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like birds, reptiles, and fish,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564160,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you find that they all follow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565360,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "roughly the same scaling relationship."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567520,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, they don't all fit\nperfectly onto the same line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569760,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the base metabolic rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571040,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for warm-blooded animals is higher"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572720,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than for cold-blooded ones,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574320,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they all scale according\nto the same power law,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577440,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mass raised to the three-quarters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579840,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some argue that this relationship\nexpands all the way down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582400,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to single cells and the molecular\nmachines inside of them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585600,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If that's true, Kleiber's Law governs life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587840,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spanning more than 25 orders of magnitude."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591520,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then the question is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593280,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if an elephant has so many more cells"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and each cell is a similar size"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598480,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a cell in a smaller creature,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600880,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and yet it's using\nproportionately less energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605040,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like it's got a lower\nmetabolic rate per pound"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608080,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or per kilo or per cell,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610720,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's really saying that those cells"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613040,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are functioning with much less energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615800,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's like there's some\nefficiency to being big,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618720,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's hard to understand why."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What is it that the cells\nare providing to each other,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624160,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "somehow cooperating in some way?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626240,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I just put in my calculator\n100 to the three quarters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629040,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you got an organism\nthat's 100 times bigger,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632080,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then according to this, only 31.6"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635760,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times the metabolic rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637840,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it seems like a big savings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640080,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's a massive improvement, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642080,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a big savings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643200,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a biological fact,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but people have been\narguing now for a century"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648080,
    "dDurationMs": 2064,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what accounts for this three quarters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650144,
    "dDurationMs": 14,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650158,
    "dDurationMs": 2322,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- In the decades following\nKleiber's observation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652480,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the mystery only deepened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654640,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Researchers discovered that\nbrain size also roughly scales"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658160,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as mass to the three quarters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659920,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so does an animal's growth rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661840,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the amount of blood pumped per minute."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664240,
    "dDurationMs": 3491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But not every property scales\nas mass to the three quarters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667731,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If you ask how long a\ncreature will live, a mammal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671520,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that tends to be proportional to its mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673760,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the one quarter power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675920,
    "dDurationMs": 2151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One over four, not three over four."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678071,
    "dDurationMs": 2089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Host] So that means if you\ndouble the mass of a mammal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680160,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then on average, its lifespan\nis around 19% longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684000,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, blood\ncirculation time also scales"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686720,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as roughly mass to the one\nquarter, while breathing rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689840,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and heart rate both scaled\nto the negative one quarter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're not all three quarters power laws,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695280,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they are all multiples of a quarter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the question on everyone's mind was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700080,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where are these quarter power\nscaling laws coming from?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703080,
    "dDurationMs": 3946,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- One popular theory emerged in the 1990s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707026,
    "dDurationMs": 1374,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\nBrian Enquist was studying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708400,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for an undergraduate degree in biology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710960,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Most of the biology\nclasses then that you take,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713440,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you learn about the Krebs Cycle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715200,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then you have to memorize\nall the different parts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717600,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a flower and then all..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719040,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have a different\nterminology for everything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720960,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Henry] But then one day\nhe took a zoology class"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723440,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where they showed him those\nquarter power scaling plots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725990,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Brian] I just couldn't believe it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727200,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I was like, \"You got to be kidding me.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729200,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, this is kind of\nlike something fundamental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 731600,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's kind of like underlying\nbiological diversity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734320,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there I knew immediately that I wanted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737040,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to kind of quit my specialized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739440,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kind of plant physiology research"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741600,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and do something associated with scaling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744560,
    "dDurationMs": 420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744980,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Henry] So Enquist started\nstudying for his PhD,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747680,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under Professor James Brown,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749120,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who had been thinking about\nscaling laws for years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751760,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they knew that often\nwhen power laws appear,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754000,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's some form of self-similarity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755600,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the underlying system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756880,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they wondered, what could\nthat self-similarity be?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759840,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they suspected that it\nmight have something to do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the way resources are\ntransported through the body,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764320,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specifically the networks that do this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766720,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had the biological intuition,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768400,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but to get a complete theory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769680,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they needed a formal\nmathematical framework."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772240,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, they\nneeded a mathematician"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774400,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a theoretical physicist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775920,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And at the time, Jim was associated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778560,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the Santa Fe Institute,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780160,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he started asking around with,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782640,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is there anyone up here\nthat's interested in these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784480,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "biological scaling relationships?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then the president at the\ntime said, \"You know what?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788960,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know of this physicist\nwho's up at Los Alamos"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792320,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who was talking about biological\nscaling relationships.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795600,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so we met Geoffrey and\nit was like immediately,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798640,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's like we'd been talking\nabout the same things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801120,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for like years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802960,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like, you know, finding,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 805120,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "someone who's been like\nspeaking your language,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807040,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but no one could understand you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808950,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Henry] So West, Brown\nand Enquist teamed up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810960,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to try and find a compelling\nexplanation for Kleiber's Law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813760,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- They started by assuming\nthree simple premises."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817440,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first premise is that the networks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819280,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that distribute resources\nare space-filling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821360,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since they need to reach\nevery cell in the body."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824320,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second premise is\nthat the terminal units"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826560,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of those networks, the thinnest segments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828560,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the outer periphery\nof the delivery system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830720,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have the same width regardless\nof the size of the organism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833760,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the outermost blood\nvessels that carry nutrients"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 836320,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to an elephant's skin\ncells are about as thick"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838560,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the ones in a mouse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840000,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The elephant just has many more of them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842720,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the third premise is that over time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844720,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "evolution has driven\nthese transport networks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846880,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "toward an efficient design."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848960,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what should such a network look like?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 851040,
    "dDurationMs": 400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 851440,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, intuitively, to get\nfuel from one place to another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854000,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as efficiently as possible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855360,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you want the path to be\nas short as possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857360,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So basically a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858960,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because fuel needs to\nreach every part of the body,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861440,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would also need many different paths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863680,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as you go to larger\nand larger organisms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865760,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the networks inside need to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867040,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reach a larger and larger volume."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869040,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One way to do this is\nto stretch all the paths"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871360,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and match the growth of the animal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873280,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, the volume of the animal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875040,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should scale as these\ninternal path lengths cubed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878080,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or if we rearrange that,\ninternal path length should scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880880,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as volume to the one-third,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882640,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just like the overall\nlength of the animal does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885440,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this design is incredibly wasteful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887920,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take these two regions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889600,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The two vessels that\nare bringing blood here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891520,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "go through almost the\nsame path in the body,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893600,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they only split up just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895200,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before they reach their destinations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897120,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If instead we had just one\nvessel up to this point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899200,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and split it only when the\npaths needed to diverge,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902080,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we could serve the two regions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903440,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "using a lot less vessel material"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905280,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a lot less blood to fill the vessels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907760,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, you can extend this logic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909280,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for all the blood vessels in the body,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910880,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you end up with a\nmuch more efficient design"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 913120,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of branching blood vessels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 915360,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now we run into another issue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917200,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because each branching point\nprovides an opportunity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919440,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for some of the blood to\nbounce back, that is reflect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922560,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you have many reflections,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924160,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would mean it\ncosts significantly more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925920,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy to pump blood around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927680,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So next, they argue that\nnature should favor structures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930080,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that minimize reflections."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931600,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as it turns out, this happens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933120,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if the cross-sectional area of the vessels"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 935360,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stays the same before\nand after the branching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937920,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you've got a cross-sectional area"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939600,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of two centimeters squared\nfor the main vessel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941680,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then each of the two\nbranches need to have an area"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943760,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of one centimeter squared each,\nfor large vessels at least."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947760,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For smaller ones, daughter\nbranches can be a bit thicker"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950480,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to allow blood to slow down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952080,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and exchange resources with\nthe tissue it's reaching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955200,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you keep repeating this\npattern across the network,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 957840,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you end up with this, a\nbranching self-similar fractal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961600,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you look at the actual shape"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963360,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the circulatory system,\nit has this geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it seemed like they\nwere onto something."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But how do you get from this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971280,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to quarter power scaling laws?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973360,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, mathematician Felix\nHausdorff discovered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975600,
    "dDurationMs": 3026,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that self-similar fractals\nhave an interesting property."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978626,
    "dDurationMs": 1294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\nTake a straight line segment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979920,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's completely one-dimensional\nand not a fractal at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982880,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hausdorff assigned this\nline segment a value of 1.0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986720,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now imagine adding a few bends"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989680,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more bends to those bends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 991680,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you keep doing this,\nthe line becomes more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993920,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more fractal-like."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995520,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Eventually, if you keep applying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996720,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the right kind of contortions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that one-dimensional line segment fills up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000000,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an entire region of the 2D plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1002800,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hausdorff assigned these\nspace-filling fractal curves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005200,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a value of 2.0, corresponding\nto their dimensionality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008880,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same ideas apply to a 2D surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011240,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So think about a piece of paper, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013920,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two-dimensional."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015040,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All then the fractal network\nis doing is crumpling up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1018240,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that sheet of paper,\nand it effectively fills"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1021120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a ball of volume."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1022720,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can now describe\nthat sheet of paper"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025120,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a sphere instead of a\ntwo-dimensional sheet of paper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029040,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Henry] Repeat the\nright pattern of folds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1030960,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at smaller and smaller\nscales, and a 2D surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033520,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fills more and more of a 3D volume."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035920,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the mathematical limit,\nit becomes space filling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038480,
    "dDurationMs": 2470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with Hausdorff dimension of 3.0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040950,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Brian] You know, biologically, I said,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1042000,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Well, what does that mean?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043200,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That enables an organism for a given size"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046560,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to pack in more of these\nmetabolic surface areas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050800,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than would be expected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's because of this\nfractal-like structure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055040,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that enables you then to pack\nin and have all of these folds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058640,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and convolutions and on top of each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061200,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to pack in an enormous\namount of membrane surfaces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064760,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- As a result, the Hausdorff\ndimension of the surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067440,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the circulatory\nsystem is roughly three,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1070400,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning its surface area doesn't scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1072240,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as its length squared,\nbut it's length cubed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075200,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since the metabolic rate hinges on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077120,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how fast resources can be\nexchanged across the surface area,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1080560,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, it must also\nscale like length cubed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083760,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But remember, West, Brown and Enquist"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1085920,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wanted to explain Kleiber's Law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1087840,
    "dDurationMs": 4546,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they needed to know how\nmetabolic rate scales with mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092386,
    "dDurationMs": 14,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092400,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since every cell needs to\nbe served by the network,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094800,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this means that the volume"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1095840,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around the network should be proportional"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097280,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the animal's mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1098720,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since volume is just\nsurface area times length"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101360,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and surface area is\nproportional to length cubed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103920,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that means both volume and mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105680,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must be proportional to\nlength to the fourth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1108240,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which can be rewritten to show\nthat length is proportional"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to mass raised to the one quarter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113040,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you plug that into the equation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1114560,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the metabolic rate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115600,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you find that the metabolic rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116960,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must be proportional to\nmass to the three-quarters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120400,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exactly as Max Kleiber had found."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1123520,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "West, Brown and Enquist\npublished their work in 1997,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126720,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it soon came to be known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128160,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as WBE Theory, after their initials."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1130680,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And the theory is quite rigid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1133440,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It makes very specific predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135840,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is good science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137280,
    "dDurationMs": 480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137760,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is sticking your neck out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1139280,
    "dDurationMs": 2856,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's an incredibly beautiful theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142136,
    "dDurationMs": 904,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\n- [Derek] Take a look at this table"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1143040,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from Geoffrey West's book."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144560,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are the scaling\nexponents WBE theory predicts,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1147520,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including many that are\nnot multiples of a quarter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150320,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but all follow from the same theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1152640,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the radius\nof an animal's aorta"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155040,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should scale with its mass\nto the three-eighths or .375."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1158960,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the area of its lungs\nshould scale with mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161440,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the 11-12ths or about 0.92."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164640,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In total, this chart makes\n26 different predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167920,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, these are the observed data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1170320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Radius of the aorta, 0.36."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1172960,
    "dDurationMs": 2549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lung area, 0.95."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1175509,
    "dDurationMs": 1531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Steven] That's the really shocking thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177040,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about what they did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177840,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had a table with\nsomething like, I don't know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "20 or 30 predictions of exotic exponents,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1183040,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's what you\nreally see in the data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1185120,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this one theory accounts not only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1186880,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the three-quarters\npower of metabolism,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189280,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but for literally dozens of other things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1191440,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that biologists have measured."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1193120,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Some of the scaling\nlaws are easy to explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196080,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "once you've got the\nthree-quarters law for metabolism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1198960,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take a mammal's heart rate, for instance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1201200,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Heart rate is equal to the blood flow rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1203200,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the amount or volume\nof blood in every beat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1205840,
    "dDurationMs": 160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1206000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The volume of blood\nper beat has been found"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208000,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to scale in direct proportion\nto an animal's mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1210560,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that's just M."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1211920,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the blood flow rate?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1213360,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, remember that\nmetabolism is all about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1215360,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how nutrients get\ndistributed around the body."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217600,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So most biologists agree metabolic rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1219520,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and blood flow rate are directly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1220880,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proportional to one another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1222160,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So heart rate should scale\nas metabolic rate over mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1225600,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Swapping in the scaling\nlaw Kleiber had found,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1228080,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that gives us M to the minus one quarter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1230640,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning bigger animals should have slower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1232640,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heartbeats than smaller ones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1234240,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is exactly what\nwe observe in nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1236880,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The world's smallest\nmammal, the Etruscan Shrew,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1239280,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has an extraordinary heart\nrate of 1200 beats per minute."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242560,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's 20 beats per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1244800,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whereas the biggest land mammal,\nthe African bush elephant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247360,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has a typical heart rate of\nonly 30 beats per minute."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1250480,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we can do something\nsimilar for lifespan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253440,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the leading theories is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1254640,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that an animal's lifespan is based on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256480,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the accumulation of metabolic damage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1258560,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, as each chunk\nof tissue in an organism"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1261520,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "processes nutrients over time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1263280,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this causes damage to accumulate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1265440,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that over time\ncauses the animal to die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1268240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the rate at which an\nanimal accumulates damage"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1270480,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is its metabolic rate per unit of mass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1272720,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its lifespan should be\nthe inverse of that rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1275600,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If damage accumulates\nfaster, it dies sooner."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1277920,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If it accumulates slower, it lives longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1280320,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So lifespan is proportional to M over B,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283360,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or substituting in Kleiber's\nLaw, M to the one quarter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1287280,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So lifespan should increase with mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1290080,
    "dDurationMs": 1826,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you do see this in nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1291906,
    "dDurationMs": 14,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1291920,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A shrew only lives for one\nto two years in the wild"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1294800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while a mighty African elephant\ncan live up to 70 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1298400,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you're a small mammal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299840,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have many heartbeats per minute,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1301360,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you live a relatively short life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1303680,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Conversely, if you're a larger mammal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305680,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your heart beats much slower\nand you live a lot longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1308680,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So it's the, you know,\nlive fast and burnout"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1312080,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and die young, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1314080,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or spend it frugally and\nlive a really long life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1317760,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But you might have also\nnoticed something else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1320320,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Heart rate scales as B over M."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322480,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it equals B over M times some constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325520,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And lifespan scales as M over B."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328240,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're inverses of each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1329920,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They scale in equal and\nopposite directions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1332800,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the total number of\nheartbeats in an animal's life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1335120,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is just the heart rate\nmultiplied by the lifespan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when you multiply these\ntwo terms, they cancel out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340800,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaving you with just a constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1342720,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that suggests that no matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1344320,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what mammal you're talking about,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1346240,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it should have roughly the\nsame number of heartbeats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1349920,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can find that number by\njust plugging in some examples."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1352880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's start with the Etruscan Shrew."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1355040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The shrew's 1200 beats per\nminute multiplied by a lifespan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1357680,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of around 1.5 years gives you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1359280,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around 950 million heartbeats"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1361440,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the course of the shrew's life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1363040,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, an African\nelephant's 30 beats per minute"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365360,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "multiplied by a lifespan\nof around 65 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1367840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gives you a little over\na billion heartbeats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371040,
    "dDurationMs": 1186,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we could keep going."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1372226,
    "dDurationMs": 2414,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(upbeat music)\nBut for nearly every mammal you look at,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1374640,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you keep landing at the same figure of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1376720,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around a billion heartbeats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1378720,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why nearly every\nmammal from a tiny field mouse"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1381840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a gazelle, from a\ncheetah to a hippopotamus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1385280,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they all get around a billion heartbeats"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1387680,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between the day they're\nborn and the day they die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1392160,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is one major outlier, one mammal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1395280,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that gets significantly more\nthan a billion heartbeats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1398640,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is us, humans.\n(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401760,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We are the lucky ones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1403680,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Three centuries ago,\nhumans were much closer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1406320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the standard value of\none billion heartbeats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1408960,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But around the mid 1800s, germ theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1411200,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and better sanitation\nmethods became widespread,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1413600,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "causing a stark decrease in\nthe number of child mortalities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1416080,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and deaths from disease."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1417600,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So life expectancy began to climb up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1419760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And with it, the average number\nof heartbeats in a lifetime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422800,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look closely, you can\nalso see some significant drops"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426080,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like this 1918 dip from\nthe Spanish flu pandemic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1429120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or over here, what appears to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1430720,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the impact of the Second World War."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432720,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But overall, the trend is clear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1434960,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have systematically\nbeen increasing the number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1437120,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of heartbeats we get in\nour lifetime to the point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439680,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where now the average human\ngets nearly three billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1442800,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heartbeats before they die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1445200,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't know if there's a\nbetter argument for science"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1447440,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and technology than this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1449120,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has literally given the average human"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1451120,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more than a full extra life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1453280,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's not just humans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1454720,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Other mammals have been observed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1456000,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to have much longer lives in\ncaptivity when they're away"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1458800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the hazards they would\nnaturally encounter in the wild."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1462000,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or if you look at it purely\nfrom the number of years we get,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1464640,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we now have the lifespan\nof a much larger mammal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1467600,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "somewhere between an elephant and a whale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471040,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is one curious\nthing about this trend."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1473280,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\nTake a look at this graph."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1475360,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It looks surprisingly similar\nto the graph from before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1478320,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, if you overlay them,\nthey look remarkably similar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1481920,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I want you to take a\nguess at what this graph is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1484880,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Have you got your answer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486880,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is the number of\npeople living in cities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1489840,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For these two charts,\nwe're using data from parts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1492400,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the United Kingdom\nwhere the record keeping"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1494560,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goes back several centuries,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1496240,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the rest of the world\nhas followed similar trends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1499520,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, that doesn't mean"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500960,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cities cause people to live longer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1503440,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it goes against the\nperception of cities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1505520,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as being full of pollution and\nbreeding grounds for disease."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1509280,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Already in 1889, a medical doctor wrote,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1512000,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"The poisonous germs and\npollutions of the city,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1514960,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's impure air and water, bad sewage,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1517840,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and endless nuisances.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1519760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do you reconcile these two views?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1522800,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or more specifically, is\nthere any quantitative data"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1525520,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on how smaller cities\ncompare to larger ones?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1528000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It turns out this is something\nthat Geoffrey West pursued"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1531280,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after his work with Brown and Enquist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1533840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He and collaborators like\nLuis Bettencourt and others"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1537280,
    "dDurationMs": 2697,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have looked at scaling laws in cities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1539977,
    "dDurationMs": 14,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1539991,
    "dDurationMs": 1449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Host] They looked at\nhow different properties"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1541440,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the amount of crime scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1543040,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the population of the city increases,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1545040,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what they found is that if you plot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546480,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "serious crimes on a log log plot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1548080,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the data clusters around a straight line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1550000,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a slope of 1.15,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1552880,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning crime grows faster\nthan linear or super linear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1556880,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for every doubling\nof a city's population,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1559120,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get around 2.2 times\nas many criminal cases"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1562880,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or around 120% more crime\nas opposed to the 100%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1567120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you might naively expect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1568720,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make matters worse, researchers found"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1570560,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the same general pattern"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1571840,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "holds for the amount of wastewater"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1573840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even the number of AIDS cases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1576320,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The exact exponents vary a little,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1578240,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but overall, as cities grow larger,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1580320,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you systematically get more of each."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583200,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it seems like that medical\ndoctor was onto something."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1586320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you might think life on\nearth would be better off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1588960,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if we all lived in small towns instead,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1591840,
    "dDurationMs": 2066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that might not be the case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1593906,
    "dDurationMs": 2814,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\nIn 2006, Dirk Helbing, Christian Kuhnert,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1596720,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Geoffrey West looked at how the number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1598720,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of gas stations scales as\na function of population."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1601280,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If a city is twice as\nbig, does it need twice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1604240,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as many gas stations?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1605600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because, you know, we have to\nsupply not exactly nutrients,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1608960,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but energy, gas, for all those cars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1611360,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Host] The naive expectation is that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1613040,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you double the number of cars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1614320,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're going to need to\ndouble the amount of fuel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1616400,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so double the gas stations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1618000,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To find out whether this was true,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1619440,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they plotted the data on a log log plot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1621280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and found a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1623280,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the exponent wasn't\none, it was about 0.8."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1627280,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that for every\ndoubling, you only need around 74%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1631200,
    "dDurationMs": 3746,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more gas stations, which\nis a decent savings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1634946,
    "dDurationMs": 2174,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\nThe amount of roads and electrical cables"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1637120,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also scale in roughly the same way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1639120,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rough figure that\nWest gives in his book"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1641120,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that they all have scaling\nexponents of around 0.85."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1643800,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It is interesting\nthat some of the things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1645920,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we can share, like you can drive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1648000,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the road, but so can I."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1649760,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it's shared resources, yes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1652000,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cities can be surprisingly green."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1654160,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The argument is that\ncities can be even greener"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1656720,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than you might think than living out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1658160,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the middle of nowhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1659240,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But cities have even bigger benefits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1662000,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Things like total wages, GDP,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1664240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the number of patents\nall scale superlinearly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1667760,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with exponents that cluster\nsomewhere around 1.15,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1671760,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning that for every doubling in size,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1673840,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get around 120% more of each."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1677520,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of this becomes especially significant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1679360,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you compare a small\ntown of say 50,000 people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1681840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a city 100 times its size"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1684320,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because infrastructure needs\nonly need to go up by a factor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1686880,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of about 50 while total wages,\nGDP, patents and inventions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691280,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they all go up by a factor of 200."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1693840,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unfortunately, disease\nand crime also go up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1696560,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the same factor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1698320,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or look at it this way,\non a per person basis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1701200,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'd only need about\nhalf the infrastructure,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1703680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while you get double all\nthe socioeconomic factors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1707200,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So cities far from being\ndetrimental to the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1709840,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they might actually be\none of our best inventions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1712480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and an indirect driver\nof a lot of scientific"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1715040,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and technological progress."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1716800,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps this is also why people often say"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1718960,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that life in the city feels faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1721360,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A feeling that seems justified"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1722960,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because researchers looked at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1724160,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how fast people walk in\ncities of different sizes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1727040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they found that\npeople literally do walk"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1729680,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "faster in larger cities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1731440,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That turns out to depend on city size."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1734720,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not just that the\nsidewalks are congested or not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1737200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just like the vibe\ngets people amped up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1740960,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They move faster in cities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1742600,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So the pace of life\nseems to be increasing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1745760,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that may come at a cost"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1747600,
    "dDurationMs": 3506,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because as one person put it,\n\"everything nowadays is ultra."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1751120,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything is being\ntranscended continually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1753120,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in thought as well as in action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1754800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No one knows himself any longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1756800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Young people are stirred\nup much too early in life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1759280,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then carried away in\nthe world of the times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1761440,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wealth and rapidity are\nwhat the world admires\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1764000,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Could it be that life\nis accelerating so fast"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1766640,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that humans won't be able to keep up?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1769120,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, probably not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1770480,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because this quote was written in 1825"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1772800,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by Wolfgang von Goethe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1774880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the past 200 years\nand probably longer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1778160,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "almost every generation has\nfelt like life was accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1781600,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet every generation has managed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1783760,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I think it's likely we can continue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1785920,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to adapt indefinitely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1787840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as cities continue to grow in size,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1790320,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of us will continue\nto reap the benefit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1792320,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of economies of scale in much the same way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1794640,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that mammals benefit from being larger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1797360,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But while WBE Theory seems to predict"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1799360,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the exponents in\nbiological scaling laws come from,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1802160,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for cities, there is no widely accepted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1804720,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explanatory theory yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1806480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Trying to explain where\nthose exponents of 0.85"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1809120,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 1.15 come from is one of\nthe big goals for theorists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1812720,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Although even WBE Theory is\nnot universally accepted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1816880,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For one, the fact it\npredicts the right exponents"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1819760,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't necessarily mean the\ntheory itself is correct."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1822880,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are a few other\ntheories that predict"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1824720,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some of the same scaling exponents,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1826880,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there are also some other critiques."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1829400,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There's a lot of discussion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1831200,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It may look convincing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1832400,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And personally, I tend to\nthink it is very impressive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1835040,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I have very good\ncolleagues like Peter Dodds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1837920,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at University of Vermont,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1839360,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he thinks that a\nlot of the data analysis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1841920,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is either not done exactly right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1843840,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or that the data are so noisy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1846160,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you shouldn't really\ntake this so seriously."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1849120,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Dodds even argues that Kleiber's Law"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1851280,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "itself might not be true.\n(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1853030,
    "dDurationMs": 6170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- In the 1960s, there's a\nsymposium on energy metabolism,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1859200,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some name like this in animals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1862240,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at the end of it, they vote 29 to zero"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1864880,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it's going to be\nthree quarters, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1866640,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because, you know, you\ngot to set some rules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1869200,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you go back and look at the data,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1870480,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which no one is really\ndoing anymore, right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1872480,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the data does not work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1873920,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like it doesn't work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1875520,
    "dDurationMs": 233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1875753,
    "dDurationMs": 1927,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Henry] This is a\ngraph of metabolic rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1877680,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a function of mass based on a study"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1879520,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that looked at 391 species of mammals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1882000,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much larger than Kleiber's range."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1883760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it looks like the three-quarter\nslope fits quite well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1886800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is just the\ntop part of the chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1888800,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the biggest mammals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1890240,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you zoom out, you see that\nthe rest of the mammals appear"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1892960,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fall on a line that's\ncloser to two-thirds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1896320,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in recent studies of bird metabolism,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1898240,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you also find a slope that appears closer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1900080,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to two-thirds than three-quarters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1902000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Could it be that those French scientists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1904000,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from centuries ago were right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1905440,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that metabolic rate really does"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1907120,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just scale with surface area?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1908960,
    "dDurationMs": 2066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, not so fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1911026,
    "dDurationMs": 1454,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(mellow music)\nFor one, many recent studies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1912480,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of cold-blooded animals find slopes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1914400,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that are significantly\nhigher than two-thirds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1916720,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bigger problem is that measuring"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1918240,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "metabolic rates is difficult."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1919840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It generally involves putting\nanimals in a container"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1922320,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and taking very precise measurements"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1923920,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their heat production\nor oxygen consumption,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1926480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all while ensuring that the\nanimal is in an unstressed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1929040,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "low activity resting state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1930960,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unsurprisingly, this is\nparticularly difficult"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1933040,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to pull off with large animals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1935120,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as a result, many studies\nhave found scaling exponents"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1937600,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the error bars include both"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1939520,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two-thirds and three-quarters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1942240,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, the research community is split."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1944080,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many uphold Kleiber's Law and\nthe three-quarter scaling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1946560,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while others think it's two-thirds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1948400,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But a growing number suspect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1949840,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that there is no\nuniversal scaling exponent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1952160,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across all of life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1953680,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, it may very well be the case"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1955280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the metabolic rate of larger mammals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1957280,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scales as their mass\nto the three-quarters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1959040,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while for smaller ones, it's\ntheir mass to the two-thirds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1961480,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You know, it's like\neverything in science"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1963680,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that there are people\narguing, and that's good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1965880,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I guess the bigger exhortation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1967520,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be someone to really measure it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1969040,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measure things beautifully."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1970240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, we're in 2026,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1972480,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has to be not just one\nelephant at one zoo,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1975520,
    "dDurationMs": 2151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it needs to be measured again really well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1977671,
    "dDurationMs": 1289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Host] What everyone does agree on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1978960,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that scaling laws are real."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1980800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Life is not linear all the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1983280,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are deals to be had."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1984640,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's often in real life\ndepartures from proportionality,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1988400,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you have to be aware of it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1990080,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sometimes things punch above their weight,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1992320,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as you get bigger,\nyou get more efficient."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1995200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sometimes there are detriments to size."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1998200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So it pays to know how things scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2001200,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Clearly from an energy\nefficiency perspective,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2003840,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "animals benefit from being larger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2006240,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, all of us potentially stand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2008160,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to gain from having more\npeople living in larger cities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2011440,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It could lead to more\ndiscoveries and inventions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2014160,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in doing so, improve\nthe standard of living"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2016480,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for all of us, which\nmight even give us more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2019680,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heartbeats in our lifetimes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2024880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From the surface law to\nKleiber's law to WBE theory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2028160,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how metabolic rate scales with mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2030080,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been one of biology's\nbiggest debates for centuries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2032560,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By collecting better data\nand analyzing it carefully,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2035440,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a good chance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2036240,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the next generation of\nresearchers could be the ones"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2038640,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to finally put this debate to rest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2040640,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It could be one of you watching\nor a student that you know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2044560,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And today's sponsor, Brilliant, is helping"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2046560,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to train the next\ngeneration of researchers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2048400,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "preparing their minds to solve the huge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2050560,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "questions they'll face."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2051760,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brilliant is a cutting edge personal tutor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2053840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that helps any student excel\nin math, science, and coding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2057840,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it comes to learning,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2059040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one-on-one tutoring really\nis the gold standard,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2061680,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this can be expensive\nand logistically difficult."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2064560,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a substitute, students\noften turn to AI for guidance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2068320,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But most AI platforms hinder learning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2070880,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by simply just giving away the answers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2073360,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead, Brilliant is\ndesigned to guide students"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2076240,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to their own aha moments\nby asking probing questions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2079200,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by breaking problems\ndown step by step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2082000,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For instance, check out what\nhappened when I launched one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2084240,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Brilliant's lessons\non rotating coordinates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2086720,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and told its tutoring tool\nthat I was struggling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2089520,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It asked me a specific follow-up question"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2091760,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even labeled relevant\npoints on the graph"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2094320,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to give me a nudge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2095840,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brilliant is an excellent\naid for the young math"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2098080,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and science learners in your life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2099920,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the kind of tool I wish\nI had when I was in school."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2103520,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So click the link below\nor scan the QR code"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2106080,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to get started with\nBrilliant's tutor for free,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2108640,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or upgrade to premium\nto unlock all courses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2111680,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And right now, Veritasium\nviewers can save 20% off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2114320,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an annual subscription at\nbrilliant.org/veritasium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2118320,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I want to thank Brilliant\nfor sponsoring this video,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2120880,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I want to thank you for watching."
    } ]
  } ]
}
